# Normalise line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# Committed history was drifting: tool-driven edits during development wrote
# CRLF into files that had been stored LF, which turns a three-line change into
# a whole-file diff and makes `git blame` useless on the affected files.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text and store it as LF; `eol=lf` means it
# is checked out as LF too, on every platform. Editors handle LF fine on Windows
# and the alternative -- per-platform checkout -- reintroduces exactly the churn
# this is meant to stop.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.tga binary
*.wav binary
*.pk3 binary
*.bsp binary
*.md3 binary
